Hi!

If you want to use this code for whatever reason, these are the instructions. 

The instructions are the same for both languages.

1. Execute download_papers.py - NOTE (This file produces a paper_list that contains the logs of the execution, if a paper says failed it means that it didnt download correclty, just do it manually, pdfs are a hassle)
2. Execute verify_pdfs - This step is necessary to ensure pdf health in order for the next steps to work.
3. Execute inject_context_single_block.py
4. Execute approach_1_single_agent.py
5. Execute evaluate_approaches.py
6. Execute download_ft_papers.py (inside finetuning folder)
7. Execute generate_raw_ft_dataset.py (inside finetuning folder)
8. Execute generate_ready_ft_dataset.py (inside the finetuning folder)
Layout note (2026-10): datasets live outside this repo at ../datasets/{english,spanish} (research/llms-chomps layout: paper/ datasets/ code/). Scripts resolve them relatively.

=====================================================================
Revision package (October 2026) — chomps/
=====================================================================
The scripts above are the competition pipeline, kept verbatim as the record of
what was submitted (their prompts are extracted byte for byte by
chomps/extract_prompts.py). Everything added for the journal revision lives in
the chomps/ package and is reproducible with:

  python3.12 -m venv ../.venv && ../.venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
  # ../.env must define AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT and AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY
  cd code
  ../.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests -q                 # offline tests (no API)
  ../.venv/bin/python common/fix_bad_pdfs.py             # after download_papers.py / verify_pdfs.py
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.retrieval                # context stores: pseudo_rag(_rerun), bm25_k*, dense_k*, full, none
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.judge --help             # judge runs -> ../results/votes/
  ../.venv/bin/python finetuning/run_finetune.py status  # fine-tuning jobs (launch/status/deploy)
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.fluency_synth            # synthetic fluency fine-tuning data
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.synth_qc --verbatim      # audit of the synthetic factuality data
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.meta --help              # meta-learner (original and CV protocols)
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.logits                   # token-logit analysis
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.retrieval_eval           # retrieval statistics + grading sheets
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.grades --workflow-json ../results/retrieval_eval/grading_workflow_result.json
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.error_attribution
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.cost
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.report                   # result tables -> ../results/tables/
  ../.venv/bin/python -m chomps.paper_tables             # LaTeX table bodies -> ../paper/tables/

Design contract: chomps/DESIGN.md. Every LLM call is cached in ../cache/llm_cache.sqlite,
so re-running any command after a crash costs nothing. Fine-tuning jobs and their
deployments are logged in finetuning/jobs.jsonl.
